---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import ds1 from '../../assets/images/design-system-1.png';
import ds2 from '../../assets/images/design-system-2.png';
import figmaComponents from '../../assets/images/figma-component-library-button-example.png';
import uofaStyleguide from '../../assets/images/uofa-styleguide.png';
---
<Layout title="Design Systems | Andrew Smith" description="RAA design system and University of Adelaide styleguide — component libraries, tokens, and documentation built for scale.">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="case-page">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="case-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><a class="breadcrumb-link" href="/portfolio/work">Work</a><span class="breadcrumb-separator">/</span><span>Design Systems</span></p>
        <h1 class="display-title">Components, tokens, and documentation built for scale.</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">A design system earns its place when it makes the right decision the easy one. The examples below cover two organisations where the system was built as infrastructure — not a side project — with governance, documentation, and adoption built in from the start.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="meta-strip">
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Organisations</p><p class="meta-value">RAA, University of Adelaide</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Role</p><p class="meta-value">Senior UX Lead, UX Manager</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Scope</p><p class="meta-value">Figma, ZeroHeight, tokens, docs</p></div>
      </section>
      <section class="lead-image-section">
        <Image class="lead-image" src={ds1} alt="RAA Apiary design system homepage in ZeroHeight showing Get started, Foundations, Components, and Patterns" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="summary-section">
        <p class="section-kicker">RAA Apiary Design System</p>
        <h2>A shared library of components, patterns, and principles.</h2>
        <div class="summary-main">
          <p>Apiary is RAA's design system — published in ZeroHeight and maintained in Figma, covering accessibility standards, design tokens, typography, layout, all UI components, and usage patterns. Every component includes an overview, usage guidelines, design specs, a changelog, and code documentation.</p>
          <p>The governance work around Apiary — getting ARB endorsement, managing the contribution process, and ensuring adoption across design and engineering — is what makes it a system rather than a library.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={ds2} alt="RAA Apiary Button component page showing anatomy, overview, usage guidelines, design specs, changelog, and code tabs" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">Figma Component Library</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>The Figma side of the system — RAADS — holds the component library with full variant coverage including regular, secondary, text, icon-only, sizes, states, and error variants. Each component is documented with usage rules directly in the Figma layers panel so designers have guidance without leaving the tool.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={figmaComponents} alt="Figma RAADS component library showing button variants across regular, secondary, and text styles with all states" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">University of Adelaide</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>Before RAA, a custom JavaScript-based styleguide application was built from scratch at the University of Adelaide — covering all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript used by every development team across the university. Before this existed, teams built independently with no shared foundation. After, consistency was a property of the system, not of individual effort.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={uofaStyleguide} alt="University of Adelaide styleguide application showing audio component documentation with HTML and JavaScript code examples" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
.case-page{position:relative;width:min(calc(100% - 3rem),78rem);margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem 0 5rem}
.eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center}
.breadcrumb-link{font-weight:600}.breadcrumb-separator{color:var(--muted-foreground)}
h1,h2{margin:0;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.05em;color:var(--foreground)}
.display-title{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.06;margin:1rem 0 0;max-width:28ch}
.hero-text,.story-block p,.summary-main p{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem}
.case-hero{padding:5rem 0 2rem}
.meta-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem;padding:1.5rem 0 .5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.meta-label{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0}
.meta-value{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700}
.lead-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem}
.lead-image,.supporting-image{width:100%;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1.5rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-large)}
.supporting-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section{padding:0 0 3rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section h2{margin-top:.75rem;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.5vw,2.2rem);max-width:32ch}
.summary-main{margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:44rem}
.section-kicker{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 .5rem}
.editorial-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:14rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:2rem;padding:3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.story-block{max-width:44rem}
</style>
